:"X-Strict-Mode: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and sends no trace context in its header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields. Without strict mode, Customer.io answers 200 for a request it drops, a key it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t know included; in it, Customer.io answers 401 for a missing or wrong key and 400","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a request it won’t process, and the destination drops and reports both. It retries no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response, a 5xx, 408 or 429. In strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch when one call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in it fails, so the encoder leaves out each call Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything else drops the whole request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it takes that in place of the address it reads from an HTTP request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_..."},{"type":"text","text":") are client keys, safe to ship in an app: they let a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client send data to the source and read nothing. Its private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_..."},{"type":"text","text":") reach every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io API, deleting people included, and must not ship in an app, so the factory"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{